   "evidence": "Basic.lean:54 is a bare `public section` and Basic.lean:205 carries no `@[expose]`; Bernstein/Basic.lean:73-74 states the repo convention (\"The body of `IsBernsteinFunction` is not `@[expose]`d, so this is how downstream files build the predicate\"). The sibling precedent Bernstein/Measures.lean:127-138 gives both `chafaiMeasure_eq_withDensity` (\"exposed as a lemma rather than an unfoldable body\") and `@[simp] chafaiMeasure_apply`; grep for `bernsteinLevyDerivativeMeasure` shows only `_apply`, `withDensity_inv_*`, `integrable_exp_neg_mul_*`, `laplaceTransform_*`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/CompletelyMonotone/Bernstein/LevyKhintchine/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Add `theorem bernsteinLevyDerivativeMeasure_eq_withDensity (\u03bc : Measure \u211d\u22650) : bernsteinLevyDerivativeMeasure \u03bc = \u03bc.withDensity (fun x : \u211d\u22650 => (x : \u211d\u22650\u221e)) := by rw [bernsteinLevyDerivativeMeasure]`, mirroring `chafaiMeasure_eq_withDensity`; instances such as `SFinite (bernsteinLevyDerivativeMeasure \u03bc)` then follow by rewriting.",
   "issue": "`bernsteinLevyDerivativeMeasure` becomes public with an unexposed body (`public section`, no `@[expose]`), and the only characteristic lemma given is `bernsteinLevyDerivativeMeasure_apply` on measurable sets. A consumer cannot reach `\u03bc.withDensity (fun x => (x : \u211d\u22650\u221e))`, hence cannot use `integrable_withDensity_iff`, `integral_withDensity_eq_integral_smul`, or obtain `SFinite`/`SigmaFinite` instances, without first re-deriving the density form via `Measure.ext`.",
   "line": 205
  }
